<pubDate>Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:28:49 GMT</pubDate>
<description>&lt;p&gt;Security forces in Kurram repelled a cross‑border infiltration, killing a Pakistani soldier and twelve militants, including Afghan Taliban fighters. The Houthi attack on Riyadh's King Khalid International Airport killed twelve civilians, prompting a Saudi‑led coalition vow of a decisive response. Afghanistan announced a potential China‑to‑Persian Gulf trade corridor, linking regional commerce to the security environment. Traders in Panjgur observed a strike, indicating domestic economic unrest. The conflict remains deadly, with 1,794 battle‑related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiywFBVV95cUxQdVZWenJrVzc4SU9uZWUtd3RFVWtIbTcxOXplbWNKTGphV2FCTmNSLTZpbWlmbm1SSWJ2OVdwV0dyOThhVVJIMW1MZVFUMUo3TGVJbEUwa0dpQnU1NnlDSE1kX2w2bzh4M1M0OGQ3UkRtY2JWVnZKdUVIVG9mUW9PQmg2V0NLYlcyUnplQ1Z1ZEVFN1FNdlJVSUpRX1YyM19EUGl2TmhTT0FzTGtnbERYaXI0eE9XWU8xdWRoUkMxMDF0TUt5ZEZ0bkxfUQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Dawn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirgFBVV95cUxNcFRvWDVSR3VUVUZxcjlMeUdyOFFDLWQ4QXNhazZSVGFMZDdEVzQxWHU0SXQtOGtSNWgxREVscTlxRFhTQXVmUXhhdjJRVnJNbWtwekVGSFVYZW9YUmlEM2x0aVY1b0VLTmx6SkZDeVlyNXNUM0VxZkYzUFNNblRfN0FwdF83d1lpS05veFN4X1NYTnp3TzRYWkRIbnplVmFZTjRRalZYZS00Mk9qZ2c?oc=5&quot;&gt;Nikkei Asia&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiSEFVX3lxTFBtU0diTTE2XzZ5cGgteXEtMEpNWkUtQllXdFJxRmVEakVMV2VNVXpjWWJXejhhMm03UjRKMW5fY3NNOGY3NEZjdw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Dawn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiSEFVX3lxTE01bWtWSGl2S2RwTnB5THhmZ3QxakNrbGZyWlhZNUZKTk9tX0xYcWpYNUlrWkxFbl90aktNSllpMHViWDE1YWVtYg?oc=5&quot;&gt;Dawn&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiSEFVX3lxTE9EcUQ4c3FPUnJoVUJVMnpDd1FJbk55X0g3U1k